; Rewrite : a view of an iota is the iota of the substituted expression.
; The iota holds its index expression at every coordinate, and the view
; reads it at the map's image of each of its own coordinates: the view is
; the iota of that expression under the map (`int-subst-of`, the view's
; map substituting the iota shape's coordinates). The bounds machinery
; then decides what it can about the substituted expression, which is how
; a slice of a concatenation learns which side it reads (select/rewrite.egg).
; The iota is minted only once the image EXISTS (an `int-subst-of` row
; exists exactly when an arm or the walk resolved it): minted on the
; demand alone, an iota over an unresolved memo node would be a spelling
; no decoder can read.
(rule
  ((= ?view (LogicalIndexMapApply (LogicalIota ?expr ?iota_shape) ?map ?shape)))
  ((int-subst-demand ?expr ?map))
  :ruleset main_ruleset
  :name "iota/rewrite: a view of an iota demands the substituted expression"
)
(rule
  (
    (= ?view (LogicalIndexMapApply (LogicalIota ?expr ?iota_shape) ?map ?shape))
    (= ?image (int-subst-of ?expr ?map))
  )
  ((union ?view (LogicalIota ?image ?shape)))
  :ruleset main_ruleset
  :name "iota/rewrite: a view of an iota is the iota of the substituted expression"
)
